{
  "_comment": "Permission catalogue. Endpoints check resource:action permissions; Keycloak (single realm) decides who has them: permissions are client roles of reeve-api, roles below are realm roles composed of them, presets bundle roles. groups is the subgroup layout created under /organisations/<orgId>; organisationRole is assigned on the organisation group itself so every member has it. Seeds/migrates Keycloak through cf-lob/keycloak-config/tools. Groups form a tree: a member of a subgroup also gets the roles of its parent groups (e.g. transactions/setup/erp = viewer + setup + erp). Publisher sits next to reviewer so review and publish can be given to different people (four-eyes).",
  "modules": [
    "transactions",
    "reporting",
    "funding"
  ],
